# tremor-script's interpreter had two `in place` fast paths for patch and
# merge (tremor-script/src/interpreter/expr.rs). `let event = patch event of
# ... end` normally clones the target, applies the operations, and assigns the
# result back; when the assignment target and the change target are the same
# path, the `up` pass in ast/raw.rs rewrote the expression to PatchInPlace /
# MergeInPlace, and the interpreter skipped the clone: it resolved the target
# to a `Cow<Value>` it had just asserted is borrowed, takes `&Value` out of
# it, and turned that shared reference into `&mut Value` with
# `mem::transmute` so the change operations could mutate the event, state,
# metadata or local storage in place. A shared reference carries no
# exclusivity, so the `&mut` is a mutable alias to storage the compiler may
# have assumed immutable -- undefined behaviour, and the memory unsafety the
# advisory reports. The change operations are user script, so a script running
# inside one operator could observe or race another reader of the same
# storage. The fixed revision deletes both fast paths: the rewrite in raw.rs always
# produces a plain assignment now, and the interpreter clones the target and
# patches the owned copy, exactly like every other assignment.
#
# The same transmute shape remains elsewhere in that file (assign_nested, the
# state/event assignment path, tracked separately upstream) and in the kafka
# source (`let s: &mut MessageStream = mem::transmute(self)`), all of them
# promoting a shared reference behind inference; the binding is keyed on the
# class, not on the two functions this advisory removed.
#
# The turbofish spelling and the `&mut`-annotated let are both real: the
# patch/merge fast paths used the annotated let (the source type is erased by
# inference), assign_nested writes through `mem::transmute::<&Value, &mut
# Value>(current)`. A `&mut`-to-`&mut` reinterpretation (same exclusivity,
# only the layout changes) and a lifetime-erasure transmute (`Script<'_>` to
# `Script<'static>`, no reference promotion) stay unlabelled.

test "tremor-script: patch_in_place transmutes a borrowed &Value into &mut"
  lang rust
  file patch_in_place.rs
  expect VYQL-MEM-009
  expect_review code.UnsafeMutableAlias
  code
  ```
  use std::borrow::Cow;
  use std::mem;

  fn patch_value<'run, 'event>(
      v: &'run mut Value<'event>,
      expr: &'run Patch<'event>,
  ) -> Result<()> {
      Ok(())
  }

  impl<'script> Expr<'script> {
      fn patch_in_place<'run, 'event>(
          expr: &'run Patch<'event>,
      ) -> Result<Cow<'run, Value<'event>>> {
          let value: Cow<'run, Value<'event>> = stry!(expr.target.run());
          debug_assert!(
              !matches!(value, Cow::Owned(_)),
              "We should never see a owned value here as patch_in_place is only ever called on existing data in event, state, meta or local"
          );
          let v: &Value<'event> = value.borrow();
          // ALLOW: https://github.com/tremor-rs/tremor-runtime/issues/1032
          #[allow(mutable_transmutes, clippy::transmute_ptr_to_ptr)]
          let v: &mut Value<'event> = unsafe { mem::transmute(v) };
          stry!(patch_value(v, expr));
          Ok(value)
      }
  }
  ```

test "tremor-script: assignment clones the target and patches the owned copy"
  lang rust
  file patch_assign.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-009
  code
  ```
  use std::borrow::Cow;

  fn patch_value<'run, 'event>(
      v: &'run mut Value<'event>,
      expr: &'run Patch<'event>,
  ) -> Result<()> {
      Ok(())
  }

  impl<'script> Expr<'script> {
      fn patch_expr<'run, 'event>(
          expr: &'run Patch<'event>,
      ) -> Result<Cow<'run, Value<'event>>> {
          let value: Cow<'run, Value<'event>> = stry!(expr.target.run());
          let mut owned: Value<'event> = value.into_owned();
          stry!(patch_value(&mut owned, expr));
          Ok(Cow::Owned(owned))
      }
  }
  ```

test "tremor-script: a state assignment writes through a transmuted &mut"
  lang rust
  file assign_nested.rs
  expect VYQL-MEM-009
  expect_review code.UnsafeMutableAlias
  code
  ```
  use std::mem;

  impl<'script> Expr<'script> {
      fn assign_nested<'run, 'event>(
          current: &'run Value<'event>,
          mut value: Value<'event>,
      ) -> Result<()> {
          unsafe {
              // ALLOW: https://github.com/tremor-rs/tremor-runtime/issues/1033
              *mem::transmute::<&Value<'event>, &mut Value<'event>>(current) = value;
          }
          Ok(())
      }
  }
  ```

test "a &mut-to-&mut reinterpretation keeps its exclusivity and stays clean"
  lang rust
  file header_bytes.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-009
  code
  ```
  #[repr(C)]
  struct Header {
      magic: u64,
      length: u32,
  }

  fn as_bytes_mut(header: &mut Header) -> &mut [u8; 128] {
      unsafe { std::mem::transmute::<&mut Header, &mut [u8; 128]>(header) }
  }
  ```

test "a lifetime-erasure transmute promotes no reference and stays clean"
  lang rust
  file script_static.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-009
  code
  ```
  use std::mem;

  struct Script<'script> {
      nodes: Vec<&'script str>,
  }

  fn into_static<'script>(structured: Script<'script>) -> Script<'static> {
      let structured = unsafe { mem::transmute::<Script<'_>, Script<'static>>(structured) };
      structured
  }
  ```
